====Internal rounding====

Tillamook has several [[phonemic]] "rounded" velar and uvular consonants, traditionally transcribed with the diacritic {{angbr IPA|ʷ}}. However, this is somewhat misleading to the true [[phonetic]] articulation of these consonants, as according to Thompson & Thompson, Tillamook lacks labial elements entirely.{{sfn|Thompson|Thompson|1966|p=316}} Instead, the acoustic quality perceived as [[labialization]] is described as an internal rounding created by a "cupping" of the tongue. 

This results in uvulars (postvelars) having a {{IPAblink|ɔ}}-like resonance, while (front) velars exhibit {{IPAblink|ɨ}} coloring. The chart above uses the ''ad hoc'' diacritics {{angbr IPA|ᵓ}} and {{angbr IPA|ᶤ}} to reflect this description and avoid the implication of true labialization. Similarly, the phoneme {{IPA|/w/}} is formed with this internal rounding, making it akin to {{IPAblink|ɰ}}.{{sfn|Thompson|Thompson|1966|p=316}}

